                  description: 'Identify sources of light to the earth Learners mention sources of light at home and at the school. Assemble different sources of light (realia and pictures): stars, torch, lantern, lightning, fireflies, forest fires, light bulbs, candle light etc. Learners identify and draw sources of light in their environment. Sort and classify sources of light as artificial or natural. Learners talk about why and when we need light. Designs an activity to block light from a torch using a cardboard to illustrate the importance of light. Discuss with learners: What will happen if there is no light on earth?'
